The arrow keys **do not scroll the whole board**. Instead they move the 2×2 moving object one cell in the indicated direction. As the object moves its cells change color in a fixed pattern (the leading edge becomes `S`, the trailing edge becomes `g`, side cells become `b`/`g`). The arrow keys also toggle the cursor in the rightmost columns: the 2×2 cursor block at the object's current row band switches between `W` and `N`.

